From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Horchynskyi <oleksahorch@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Port Xenia Canary ZPD occlusion queries (Vulkan host render
 targets)

Replaces ReXGlue's occlusion query handling with Xenia Canary's design
(fbd620c22 "Implement ZPD occlusion queries", 3d233a5b2 "Rewrite ZPD as a
running sample counter"): every EVENT_WRITE_ZPD snapshots a free-running
sample counter, intervals between events are measured with native Vulkan
occlusion queries split at render pass and submission boundaries, and
results are read back without stalling. New cvar occlusion_query
(fake/fast/fast-alt/strict, default fast); the fake mode keeps Canary
b447699a5's 100..80 cycling count (occlusion_query_fake_lower/upper_threshold).

Not ported: VIZ_QUERY, occlusion_query_full_counters, FSI counter buffers
(FSI and D3D12 fall back to fake counts). Query slots are reset on the GPU
after their results are copied instead of with VK_EXT_host_query_reset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
